      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let $\\alpha = a + bi$ and $\\beta = a - bi,$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.  Then \\[\\frac{\\alpha}{\\beta^2} = \\frac{a + bi}{(a - bi)^2} = \\frac{a + bi}{a^2 - 2abi - b^2}.\\]Multiplying the numerator and denominator by $a^2 + 2abi+b^2,$ we get \\[\\frac{(a + bi)(a^2 + 2abi + b^2)}{a^2 + 2abi - b^2} = \\frac{a^3 + 2a^2bi - b^3 - 2abi + 2ab^2i - 2ab^2i + 2abi}{a^2 - b^2 + 2abi - 2abi - 2abi} = \\frac{a^3 - b^3 + 2a^2bi - 2ab^2i}{a^2 - b^2}.\\]If this complex number is real, then the real part is equal to the imaginary part, so $2a^2b - 2ab^2 = b(a^3 - b^3).$  Dividing by $b$ gives $2a^2 - 2ab - a^3 + b^3 = 0.$  Completing the square gives $(2a - b)^2 - b^2 = 0,$ so $(2a - b - b)(2a - b + b) = 0,$ and $2a - b = \\pm b.$  If $2a < b,$ then $2a - b = b,$ so $a = 0.$  If $2a > b,$ then $2a - b = -b,$ so $a = 0.$  If $2a = b,$ then there is no contradiction.  Therefore, $a = 0$ and $b \\neq 0,$ which means $\\alpha = bi.$  Hence, $|\\alpha| = \\boxed{b}.$The answer is: 1",
